            <h2>Patagonia: Glaciers and granite peaks</h2>
            <p>Patagonia is the bottom of the world, with granite peaks, blue glaciers, and a lot of wind. This route goes back and forth between Chile and Argentina for the three most famous hikes in the region. Then it ends in Ushuaia, the southernmost city in the world.</p>

            <figure>
                <img src="img/placeholder.jpg" width="640" height="360" alt="Placeholder image">
                <figcaption>Photo coming soon. Stops: Torres del Paine, El Chaltén, Perito Moreno Glacier.</figcaption>
