            <div class="details">
                <section>
                    <h3 id="stay-title">Where to stay</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Torres del Paine: refugios (mountain huts) and campsites along the W, which must be booked in advance</li>
                        <li>El Calafate: hostels in town with glacier tour pickups</li>
                        <li>El Chaltén: hostels and campsites at the trailheads</li>
                        <li>Ushuaia: hostels with views over the Beagle Channel</li>
                    </ul>
                </section>

                <aside>
                    <h3 id="glance-title">At a glance</h3>
                    <div class="glance">
                        <p><strong>Best time:</strong> November to March, Patagonia's summer, with long days and the mildest weather. Pack for wind any time.</p>
                        <p><strong>Daily budget:</strong> About $70–120 per person per day. Chile is pricier than Argentina.</p>
                        <p><strong>Getting around:</strong> Long-distance buses (Bus-Sur, Taqsa) between towns, and a flight to Ushuaia.</p>
                        <p><strong>Fly in / fly out:</strong> Arrive in Punta Arenas (PUQ) and leave from Ushuaia (USH).</p>
                    </div>
                </aside>
